WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.480
Victor! Hey, Victor! Where the hell are you?!

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.480
3/15 16:24

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.150
Get out here, damn it!

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.070
Your son is worried to death about you!

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.740
Would you please stop? This is humiliating.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.900
There's nothing to be humiliated about!

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.040
This is no different than a 
son worrying about his dad!

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.590
What's wrong with a big brother 
worrying about his little brother?

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.040
Don't just decide I'm your little brother!

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.590
Ah, I commend you on a job 
well done, Kiri and Blaze.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.020
Victor is safe as well, 
so please don't worry.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.760
You have now completed your test.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.560
Test?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.980
Oh, now, don't make that face.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.850
This wasn't what I wanted, either.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:20.300
But the master ordered me to 
test the extent of your skills.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.240
I had no choice but to set all this up.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.450
Well, now you know.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.460
I realize this is upsetting to you,

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.590
but my beloved school uniforms were 
taken hostage! I had no choice!

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.930
<i>Is there no one remotely normal in Chronos?</i>

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.870
Now, all joking aside...

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.390
Kiri, you and Victor have come here

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.580
in search of his past, correct?

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.070
More specifically, you want

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.270
to acquire the record of Victor's work here.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:56.330
That's right.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.530
That record is indeed kept here.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.770
But everything in it was 
written in strange characters

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.430
that may or may not be some sort of code.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.240
Chronos's technology division 
has been trying to analyze it,

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.750
but we've yet to uncover 
a way to decipher it.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.950
Since he was rarely present at headquarters,

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.380
Victor was, and always has been, 
a man of many mysteries.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.690
We didn't even know he had a son.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:31.200
So all I can tell you at this time is that 
we don't know anything about his past.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.530
I do apologize.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.400
<i>I guess it really won't be that simple.</i>

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:43.780
He is currently working with the technology 
division to attempt to decipher his record.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.590
Perhaps he, himself, may be able to read it.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.130
Victor can?

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.910
<i>He really is desperate</i>

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.320
<i>to get back the time and memories 
that were taken from him.</i>

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.970
Oh, Kiri!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.470
Glad to see you're safe.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.790
The technology division's nothing but babes.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.180
Care to join us?

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.090
Oh? Who's this?

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:15.560
This is my pure-hearted son, dear Stiller.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.020
I told you, my name is Wendy.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.610
Was twelve years long enough
for you to forget?

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.530
Sorry about that. I'll write it down.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.220
And what about the little cutie over there?

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.240
Um, my name is Laner.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.880
I was still a young child twelve years ago,

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.510
so you might not remember me.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.620
I would never forget a beauty like you.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.050
Gosh, Victor, you're embarrassing me!

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.930
And how about the blonde there?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.090
My name's Isabele.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:49.970
Um... is the promise you made that night 
twelve years ago still in effect?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.950
Huh? What promise?

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:56.260
You're going to make me 
say it? You're so mean...

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.850
You old lecher!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.910
Just die already!

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.410
Dear me. I'm working, you know.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.790
Or are you jealous, you mopey boy?

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.280
MB for short.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.350
Give me that!

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.660
I'll decipher it!

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.910
<i>It's no use. I can't see any 
logic or regularity in it.</i>

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.460
<i>I can't entrust this to Victor.</i>

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.170
<i>I'll have to do it.</i>

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:25.540
Snake, I'd like to ask you a 
question about Horologues.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.680
What would that be?

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:30.060
A few days ago, in a town 
called C'est La Vie,

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.680
we encountered the Horologue 
that took Victor's time.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.560
It was enormous and white all over.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:38.850
It could even speak.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:42.360
It was clearly nothing like the 
Horologues we'd encountered before.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.570
Have any Horologues like 
that ever appeared before?

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.410
All white and able to speak...

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:53.450
I'm sorry, but I haven't heard of any 
accounts that might answer your question.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:55.350
Except...

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:56.410
Except?

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.340
I have had a few encounters with Horologues 
that had linguistic capabilities.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:06.480
As you know, the principal diet 
of Horologues is human time.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:10.050
They act instinctively and 
have no will of their own.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.590
But it seems that, with every 
bit of time they consume,

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.230
they also take in a proportionate 
amount of memories,

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:19.690
which eventually leads to the 
development of consciousness.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:24.230
Of course, a thousand years' worth of 
time makes a Horologue animal-like,

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.640
and at that stage,
the sprouting of simple emotions

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.550
and emergence of learning 
ability have been observed.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:33.650
And once they've consumed five 
thousand years' worth of time,

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:37.960
it's said that they can understand human 
language and even speak with them.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.880
But this is only what I've 
seen in written accounts

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.140
and heard directly from our master.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:49.720
In twenty years, I have not encountered 
a Horologue that could speak.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.500
I see.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.220
Do you believe

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.300
that if you defeat the Horologue 
that consumed Victor's time,

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.480
you can regain the time he's lost?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:05.480
I thought as much.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.410
I can't deny that.
If you defeat a Horologue,

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.610
it may be possible to reclaim 
the time that it had devoured.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.980
In particular, if you defeat one 
that has just recently fed,

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:19.250
there is data pointing to a high probability 
that the time it had eaten can be reclaimed.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.890
But if too much time passes 
after it has been consumed,

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.750
recovery is no longer possible.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.790
There is no precedent for time 
being reclaimed after that point.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:33.500
Realistically, how long might one have to 
recover time once a Horologue has taken it?

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:40.520
The time limit we have arrived at after 
many years of experimentation is...

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.980
sixty seconds, maximum.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.800
<i>Time can only be reclaimed</i>

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.660
<i>if the Horologue is defeated within 
sixty seconds after consuming it...</i>

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.910
<i>Doesn't that mean it's hopeless?</i>

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:06.840
<i>Is that Victor's room?</i>

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:17.050
Victor, I'm coming in.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:27.770
Victor?

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.490
Oh, it's you, Kiri. You're still up?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.740
Good timing. I was just starting 
to get a clear picture.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.370
You mean you actually deciphered it?!

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.870
Yep. These characters were my 
own suggestion a long time ago.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.130
Each symbol represents three 
letters of the alphabet.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.520
Is there some sort of rule 
for how they're assigned?

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.010
These are all girls' names.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.490
I wrote the names of all the 
girls I met that year in order

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.590
and assigned one character 
to every three letters.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.050
I get it!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:02.890
You were trying to decipher your 
memories of twelve years ago earlier!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.690
That's why you were getting the 
names of girls you met back then!

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.490
Exactly!

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.990
I wasn't just playing around.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:12.360
I was gathering information, 
in all seriousness.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.980
Of course, while I did decipher it,

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.400
it was all stuff about girls.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:22.610
There was hardly anything in 
it about the work I did here.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:24.370
Oh, come on!

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.600
But this day here...

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.010
July 21st, 2002.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:31.750
This is the only date 
with a detailed record.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.490
Six days before it happened!

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.590
Which means this is...

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:40.730
Yes. It was the last mission I carried out.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.080
Great! Then there must be 
some other clues here!

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.700
Like the location and mission description,

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.420
as well as information 
on the white Horologue!

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.480
Yeah. In fact, I did find 
something of interest.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.810
Records from the plane you boarded 
on the day of the mission!

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:00.060
It has the airport, the time of your flight,
and your ticket information, too.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.490
The destination was...

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:03.790
Couljours?

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:05.950
My hometown.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:24.850
Darling!

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:26.560
Got a second?

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:30.610
Darling?

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:40.420
What brings you here? And why so formal?

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:42.530
I just came to say goodbye.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.040
I found information about twelve years ago.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:48.040
I'm thinking of going to Couljours.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:52.250
I see. Well, I wish you the best.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:57.410
Snake told me something about 
this UNIQUE in my chest.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:01.010
He said that with it, the battle against 
the Horologues could quickly end.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:05.010
I realize that, but...

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.520
Just give me one month.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.600
If I fail to reclaim my time 
from the Horologue by then,

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.110
I swear to return UNIQUE to you.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.740
A commendable attitude.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:23.070
Don't worry. Even if UNIQUE is returned,

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:26.040
it would only increase my 
own fighting capability.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.790
It wouldn't have much of an 
effect in the strategic sense.

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:33.220
Since the new Oath of Time 
model came into use,

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:36.420
our agents have been returning home 
alive at a vastly increased rate.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.880
There's still room for 
more research, of course,

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.880
but at a tactical level,
that's more than good enough.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:43.970
So don't feel too bad.

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:47.920
I see. I understand now.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.150
There's one more thing 
I'd like you to tell me.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.200
Is Mina really my wife?

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.230
Something's always felt off about it.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.610
If she were really my wife,

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:04.080
wouldn't she be trying harder to 
help me get my lost time back?

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.830
But she was different.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:11.390
Let's build a new future together!

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:18.590
Actually, I had DNA tests 
done on Mina and Kiri.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.010
In utmost secrecy, of course.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:23.590
The result:

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:26.220
those two are not blood relatives.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.570
I see...

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:30.700
So that means she's not my wife, either.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.160
We can't be certain of that.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.810
Mina's genes aren't like 
those of normal people.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:39.080
Descendants of Chronos, the god of time,

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.970
experience a change in their 
DNA when they turn 18.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.760
They also cease to age,

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.830
and their blood takes on the 
ability to purify Horologues.

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:51.650
They become something completely inhuman.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:55.500
Now you see why she wasn't affected 
by the Horologue's bite, do you not?

00:12:56.690 --> 00:13:03.170
So you're saying we'll need to 
test Kiri's DNA once he turns 18

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.930
in order to find out for sure if 
he's related by blood to Mina?

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:12.650
Which means even you can't say for 
sure whether Mina is my wife or not.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:17.520
Long ago, when you and Mina were a team...

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:23.320
She kept saying she wanted to 
marry you and have a child.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.680
But even though I knew how 
badly she wanted a family,

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.600
I could not give her my support.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:34.460
So, of course, I turned 
a deaf ear to her pleas.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:37.280
And after you went missing,

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:40.460
I was sure that her zeal 
would eventually fade.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:46.490
But once she learned that you were alive,

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.940
the look on her face...

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:52.930
was that of a wife who had always 
believed her husband was alive

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.400
and waited for him.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:58.750
I don't know whether you two are 
truly husband and wife or not.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:13:59.860
But...

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.820
Her love for you is real.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.420
I realized then

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.950
that there would be no point in killing you.

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:13.160
That it wasn't within my power 
to sever the love between you.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.290
So please...

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:23.300
I want you to release Mina from 
the curse that you are to her.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:27.050
She has a duty to fulfill 
as a descendant of Chronos.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.510
Human emotions will cloud her 
resolve as a member of Chronos.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.100
That is one thing I cannot abide.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:35.860
So...

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.660
I don't care how you choose to do it.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:41.770
Just open Mina's eyes.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.780
I'm afraid I can't promise that.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.340
Sorry to say so after you've 
gone to such lengths,

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:49.410
but I'm human, too.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:53.410
If Mina isn't really my wife,
we'll cross that bridge when we come to it.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:56.050
But if she <i>is</i> my wife,

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:59.180
as a husband, my only concern is to 
give her all the love I have.

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:02.290
I see...

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.010
<i>I can't move!</i>

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.380
But I still have high hopes

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:14.180
that Mina will be released from her curse.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.970
Otherwise,

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:21.020
you will experience a despair 
more terrifying than death.

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:18.230
Wonderful Nightmare

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.030
<i>I should be outside the 
range of her control...</i>

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:29.280
<i>But everything in the space 
around me is Slowed Down!</i>

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.910
<i>Was she going easy on me last time?</i>

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.970
Threatening me won't change 
my position on the matter.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.610
So long as Mina loves me,

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:42.920
it's my obligation to return her love.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.240
Then what if Mina has a change of heart?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.450
I can swear to you that I 
won't try to chase her.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.870
I like people who catch on quickly.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:01.350
I expect the best, Victor.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.360
<i>Damn, she's a cunning woman.</i>

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:22.090
You're leaving already?

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:24.080
That was awfully fast.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:28.800
I was hoping to have a nice, leisurely 
chat with Victor about school uniforms.

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.800
Well, we actually managed to find a lead!

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.430
We can't just sit around! Right, Victor?

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.140
You're coming, too?

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.100
Of course! My sister gave her approval!

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:43.600
Well, I'm glad my farewell 
gift arrived in time.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:48.100
Those new outfits look 
wonderful on you both.

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.610
Your old ones were quite the 
worse for wear, after all.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:55.070
And in here are some funds and 
items to use in your travels,

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:58.830
some powered-up cards, courtesy of 
our technological division, and...

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.830
My top-recommended high 
school girl's uniform!

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:07.580
Anyway, with this, you are now 
official members of Chronos!

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.930
Also, at the master's orders...

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.090
I hereby name Victor the Seventh Guardian,

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.050
and grant him the title "Ace Ruler."

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:21.160
I hereby name Kiri the Third Guardian.

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:25.690
He will inherit the title of his predecessor 
who died in the line of duty: "Splash Ruler."

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.190
Guardian?

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.650
It's short for "Divine Guardian Rulers."

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.880
The name given to the top 
twelve members of Chronos

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.830
chosen by the master for the 
strength of their rule,

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.780
use of tactics, and other accomplishments.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.780
By the way, Mina...

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.120
and Blaze are Guardians, as well.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:52.070
Divine Ruler Guardians are 
dispersed throughout the world,

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:54.800
each carrying out greatly 
important missions.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:59.260
More than 70% of Horologue subjugation 
is carried out by the Twelve Guardians.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:03.300
Some have even defeated more of 
them than the master herself.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.680
They are truly the best of the best!

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:09.890
And now you are also Chronos 
Rulers recognized by the master.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:14.050
Make sure you spare no effort in 
reclaiming Victor's lost time!

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:20.950
By the way, Mina...

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.470
I need to return this to you.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.160
I'm sorry.

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.220
I don't need one that 
you've had your hands on.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.170
I got a brand new one!

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:37.570
I can't believe you'd give a 
used one to your own mother!

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:41.550
You said it! Kids these days have 
no respect for their elders!

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.380
Honestly, what are we going to do with you?

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:46.110
<i>Endure it... Endure it!</i>

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:46.430
Hey...

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.120
Let's just ignore him, Darling.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:53.440
Yeah. We need to get my time back.

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:56.740
As soon as we do, I'll be yours alone.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:06.570
What if I'm not your real wife?

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:10.020
You worry about Kiri because 
you're his father,

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:12.830
and you're kind to me
because you're my husband.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.380
You only do all that because you 
feel it's your responsibility.

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:21.510
Just like my sister. It's all about "duty."

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.010
I don't need that kind of love!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:28.430
I want you to love me from 
the bottom of your heart!

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:31.200
Not because I'm your wife,
or out of duty or obligation.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.520
I don't need that!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.600
I want you to love me for who I am!

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:49.750
<i>Mina...</i>

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:54.080
<i>Even if you truly are Victor's wife,</i>

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:57.960
<i>he will never love you from 
the bottom of his heart.</i>

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.220
<i>You will surely realize 
that on this journey.</i>

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.180
<i>We, the descendants of Chronos,</i>

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:06.790
<i>must never give our hearts to anyone.</i>

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:12.080
<i>If you do, you'll be the one 
to get hurt in the end.</i>

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:16.560
<i>Yes, just like I was long ago...</i>

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:25.820
<i>Passengers departing on the 
2:30 flight to Couljours,</i>

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:29.990
<i>if you have not checked in for your 
flight, please do so quickly.</i>

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.660
<i>Th-The air feels so heavy!</i>

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.030
<i>Someone say something!</i>

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:39.710
<i>Any other time, they'd act like a dumb 
lovey couple and make up in no time!</i>

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:42.410
There, there, honey. Don't be angry.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:44.470
Oh, darling, honestly!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.800
<i>Someone do something, please!</i>

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.600
<i>I don't care who at this point!</i>

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.640
<b>Worst in the World</b>

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.640
You idiot! Were you just 
gonna leave me behind?!

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:55.480
Didn't I tell you I'd beat the 
crap out of that white Horologue?

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:58.860
Your big brother is a man of his word!

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:02.490
<i>Why did you have to show up?!</i>

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:06.580
What are you doing here, Blaze?
No one invited you!

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.660
Shut up, you stupid little girl!

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:11.090
Yo, you're Victor, right?

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.980
Ain't this your woman?!

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:16.830
So catch her and stop being selfish,
you dumbass!

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:19.120
Well, let's get going!

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:21.340
Kiri, grab your big brother's luggage!

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:24.620
<i>He really goes at his own pace...</i>

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.880
<i>Really, he was a big help, though.</i>

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.840
Your luggage is full of nothing but snacks!

00:21:33.840 --> 00:21:35.600
Do you think this is a school field trip?

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.350
Shut up, little brother!

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:39.070
Come on, let's go!

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.070
Let's go, darling.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:42.780
Sure.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:51.490
Will and Representation

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.700
Will and Representation

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:54.750
Will and Representation

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:40.100
The Poverty of Philosophy
